*Figure 9* shows a $200\ \mu\mathrm{H}$ inductor, a $10\ \Omega$ resistor and a variable capacitor connected in series with a $0.10\ \mathrm{V}$ (r.m.s. value), $1.0\ \mathrm{MHz}$ supply. The inductor has an inductance of $200\ \mu\mathrm{H}$.

![fig-4](gce-al-physics-2020-p2-officiel-cameroun_exercice_6_fig_4.png)

At resonance, determine:

(i) the capacitance of the variable capacitor;

(ii) the current flowing in the circuit;

(iii) the voltage across the inductor;

(iv) the voltage across the capacitor.
